Jukka Lahtinen wrote:
> Hmm.. for piles of objects, the object on top is shown. And a tap is
> hardly ever OVER any objects, maybe except for a falling rock trap which I
> imagine being in the ceiling. So it is logical that objects are shown
> above traps. Anyway, things are not always logical in Nethack :-)

I figure that this patch is perfectly fine since:
a) trap display is entirely based on memory anyway; an unknown trap is
invisible regardless of objects, and a visible trap is visible due to
memory, and memory shouldn't be affected by objects that happen to be
in the same square as a trap
b) this patch doesn't provide anything you can't get by spamming the ^
command on any object you might step on. It just makes life easier.
(And the ^ command is more powerful - it shows traps under monsters
too)
c) the traps most commonly hidden by objects are: pits (when the items
are *in* the pits anyway, so the pit should definitely be visible if
the items are), and dart/arrow traps (when a pile of darts/arrows would
probably jog the hero's memory...)

> The patch will invalidate existing bones and save files because you added
> the trap_on_top flag to struct flag. If it were in struct instance_flags
> instead, it wouldn't affect file compatibility.
> The flags in instance_flags are not saved in the save file, the game only
> reads them from the configuration file and, depending on the optflags
> defined in options.c, they may be settable with the O command from within
> the game.

Thanks a lot! This was something I suspected but wasn't sure about.

